# Dead Letter Office
#
# Two rules for editing this file:
#   1. No Godot 3 entries. This project targets Godot 4.7 only and there is no
#      compatibility target (docs/CODING-STANDARDS.md §1.1). Most .gitignore
#      snippets you will find online are for Godot 3 and quietly bring
#      `.mono/`, `data_*/` and `export.cfg` with them.
#   2. No unanchored broad patterns. A pattern like `data_*/` matches at every
#      depth, and content silently failing to commit is a worse outcome than a
#      little untracked noise.

# ── Godot 4 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Import cache and editor state. Rebuilt on first open of a fresh clone.
.godot/

# Compiled by the editor from the CSV source.
*.translation

# Generated on demand by "Install Android Build Template".
/src/Dlo.Game/android/

# Keystore passwords, notarisation and store credentials. Godot 4 keeps these
# in their own file specifically so that export_presets.cfg can be committed —
# see the note below.
export_credentials.cfg

# The Steamworks SDK reads its app id from Steam when Steam launches the game, and
# from this file beside the executable when anything else does - the editor, a test
# run, a double-click. E0-01 needs one containing 480 (Spacewar, Valve's public test
# app; see SteamTransport). It is ignored rather than committed for one reason: it
# must NEVER be exported. A shipped steam_appid.txt overrides what Steam says the app
# is, and that failure is silent right up until it is a launch-day incident.
steam_appid.txt

# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#
#   *.import           Each asset's UID and import settings — pixel-art filter
#                      off, compression mode, and so on. Losing them re-imports
#                      the whole project with defaults, which silently undoes
#                      every per-asset decision.
#
#   export_presets.cfg E18 automates builds for Windows, Linux and macOS, and
#                      CI cannot export without the presets. The secrets that
#                      used to make this file unsafe to commit now live in
#                      export_credentials.cfg above.

# ── Generated placeholder assets ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Fully derived from the asset specification (docs/asset-specification.md, E17)
# via `dotnet run --project tools/Dlo.ContentTool -- generate`. The house project
# committed its generated placeholders and it cost more than it saved: every
# asset went through Git LFS (a clone that skipped `git lfs pull` booted into an
# invisible game), and the bytes were toolchain-coupled — its net8 to net10 move
# rewrote all 66 PNGs without changing one pixel, because .NET 9 swapped its
# deflate for zlib-ng. E17 carries the rule; this file is the mechanism.
#
# Directory.Build.targets regenerates these before the game builds, so a fresh
# clone still just works. When the commissioned art lands it replaces these and
# IS committed — it is authored, not derived, and cannot be regenerated.
#
# Anchored to exact paths and matched by extension rather than by directory:
# the .import sidecars in these same folders must stay tracked, because they
# carry the stable uid:// that the .tres content files resolve against.
/src/Dlo.Game/art/placeholder/**/*.png
/src/Dlo.Game/art/standin/**/*.png
/src/Dlo.Game/audio/placeholder/*.wav
/src/Dlo.Game/art/placeholder/manifest.json
/src/Dlo.Game/art/standin/manifest.json

# ── .NET ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

bin/
obj/
artifacts/
TestResults/
*.trx

# ── Editors and tooling ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

*.user
*.suo
*.userprefs
*.sln.DotSettings.user
.idea/
.vs/

# Personal editor state. If the team wants a shared config, un-ignore the
# specific file — for example `!.vscode/extensions.json` — rather than tracking
# the whole directory.
.vscode/

# ── Build and export output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Anchored to the repo root: these are where builds are written, not a pattern
# that could match a source directory somewhere deeper.
/build/
/exports/

# ── OS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# ── Transient ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

*.tmp
*.temp
*.log

# Godot's backup when it rewrites a .csproj it did not like (E14-05 watched it happen
# live, mid-test-run). Regenerated freely, never worth a diff.
*.csproj.old

# GdUnit4's generated Godot-runtime test runner. The adapter installs it into whichever
# Godot project it is running, on every run (E14-05).
gdunit4_testadapter_v5/
